This PR introduces a TypeScript port of the Python computer library cloud provider, providing the same functionality for controlling virtual machines and computer interfaces.

It also reorganizes the `libs` directory into `libs/python` and `libs/typescript` subdirectories for future typescript ports. 

It has been tested with a linux c/ua cloud container & a local macOS VM.


## Changes Included
- Cloud computer provider for 
- Interface for interacting with Linux, MacOS, and Windows based cua-computer-server
- Unit tests for all major components

## Example Usage

```ts
// NOTE: this package is not yet published on npm. Instead import `index.ts` from the `src` directory.
import { Computer, OSType } from "@cua/computer"; 

const apiKey =
  "your-cloud-api-key";

const computer = new Computer({
  osType: OSType.LINUX,
  apiKey,
  name: "your-cloud-vm-name",
});

try {
  await computer.run();
  await computer.interface.connect();
  await computer.interface.createDir("~/Desktop/example_dir");
  await computer.interface.leftClick(10, 2);
} catch (e) {
  console.log("Computer Error", e);
} finally {
  await computer.stop();
}



```

